// Title: Add Debugger Entry To AeDebug For Persistence
// Sigma ID: 092af964-4233-4373-b4ba-d86ea2890288
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects when an attacker adds a new "Debugger" value to the "AeDebug" key in order to achieve
//   persistence which will get invoked when an application crashes
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the key to setup a debugger. Which is often the case on developers machines
// References:
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/aedebug.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/configuring-automatic-debugging
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_aedebug_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AeDebug\\Debugger" and RegistryValueData endswith ".dll") and (not(RegistryValueData =~ "\"C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\vsjitdebugger.exe\" -p %ld -e %ld -j 0x%p"))
